WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.800
The internet has a lot of&nbsp;
thoughts about Keanu Reeves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.960
and so does Bridget Moynahan. So is the star&nbsp;
of "The Matrix" really as nice as he seems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.520
or are there some skeletons in his closet?&nbsp;
Moynahan's revelations may surprise you.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.360
When you've worked in Hollywood for as long as&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves has, your reputation follows you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.040
around everywhere. And in the case of movie&nbsp;
stars, the public gets to have an opinion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.560
about an actor's on-the-job behavior even&nbsp;
if they don't have any direct experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.720
working with them. In the case of Reeves, his&nbsp;
general reputation seems to be that of a quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.240
humble, decent guy, who happens to be&nbsp;
one of the most famous people on Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.520
Of course, it helps when he partakes in&nbsp;
delightful interviews where he answers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.720
questions like a normal person and has&nbsp;
viral stories come out of the woodwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.720
about what a down-to-earth person he is.&nbsp;
But is this reputation really accurate?

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:44.480
Every once in a while, someone who's worked with a&nbsp;
star like Reeves will give us a tidbit about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.320
the experience was like. Bridget Moynahan,&nbsp;
best known today as one of the stars of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:53.040
police drama "Blue Bloods," worked with Reeves&nbsp;
on both "John Wick" in 2014, and the sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.840
"John Wick: Chapter 2," in 2017. She played&nbsp;
his deceased wife, Helen Wick, whose final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.720
act prior to her passing is gifting John a dog&nbsp;
so that he won't be as alone after she's gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.200
As anyone who's seen the movies can attest,&nbsp;
that dog plays a pretty central role. And during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.080
a 2014 interview, she wasn't shy to share her&nbsp;
impressions of what Reeves was like on the set.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.080
Moynahan is no stranger to sharing the screen&nbsp;
with some of the biggest names in the business.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:20.640
After all, she joins Tom Selleck and Donnie&nbsp;
Wahlberg on "Blue Bloods." With a resume that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.360
also includes the likes of "Serendipity" and "Sex&nbsp;
and the City," it's safe to say Moynahan has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.920
around the block a few times and generally knows&nbsp;
what to expect when working with A-list stars.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:34.400
During her interview with AOL, Moynahan was asked&nbsp;
about a bevy of her famous collaborators over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.600
years, including Al Pacino and, of course, Keanu&nbsp;
Reeves. When asked about how her experience of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.840
working with Reeves on "John Wick" was, compared&nbsp;
to what she expected, Moynahan revealed,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.240
"He's very quiet and very private. I had always&nbsp;
heard that about him, and he kind of still was."

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.480
"We had a really nice time. We were playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.280
a couple that was in love so&nbsp;
that was really fun to do."

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.960
It sounds like Moynahan didn't get a chance to&nbsp;
get to know Reeves too well, despite playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.840
the assassin's late wife in flashbacks. It makes&nbsp;
sense given her role is killed off pretty early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.920
in the film, so she probably didn't spend too&nbsp;
much time getting to know the legendary actor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.840
But it also seems that her experience working&nbsp;
with Reeves was a positive one. He is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.440
after all, one of the co-stars that caused&nbsp;
Moynahan to declare during her interview,

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.160
"I have worked with the&nbsp;
best guys in the business."

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:20.080
When it comes to actors, one of the first things&nbsp;
people want to know is whether they're nice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.000
There are so many horror stories of celebrities&nbsp;
acting like divas and treating everyone they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.560
perceive as beneath them like trash. Fortunately,&nbsp;
it doesn't appear as though Reeves falls in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.480
this camp as several of his co-stars have&nbsp;
nothing but kind things to say about him.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.080
First, there's his "John Wick 3" partner&nbsp;
Halle Berry, who took to Instagram&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.320
to gush over working with Reeves on the project.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Lance Reddick, who's played Charon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.320
in all three "John Wick" movies to date, had&nbsp;
nothing but nice things to say, either. The actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:48.720
described what a consummate professional Reeves&nbsp;
was on-set and even went so far as to declare,

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:52.240
"Whenever I work with a big movie star for&nbsp;
the first time, I keep my guard up to protect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.720
my work from an ego. And if there's any big&nbsp;
movie star who's not that person, it's Keanu."

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.640
It appears that if you're going to star alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.800
any A-list celebrity in a major motion&nbsp;
picture, you want it to be Keanu Reeves.

